## Building Arctic Engine Projects

Buildable projects: `wizard/`, `tests/`, `benchmark/`, `filetest/`, `fuzz_tests/`, `antarctica_pyramids/`, and a project made by the wizard. Do not try to build `engine/` or `template_project_name/` directly -- they are not standalone targets.

Always chain cmake/make/run in a single shell command using `&&` to avoid multiple permission prompts.

In-source build, the usual one here (also the one to use when in doubt, since the existing build directories in this tree are in-source):

```
cd wizard && cmake . && make -j 8
```

Incremental rebuild after source edits only:

```
cd wizard && make -j 8
```

An out-of-source build works too, and it copies `data/` next to the binary so the program finds its assets:

```
cd wizard && cmake -B build && cmake --build build -j 8
```

The engine needs clang; CMake looks for `clang++` in the PATH unless `CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER` or `CXX` says otherwise, and it stops with a clear message when there is no clang at all. gcc is not supported.

On macOS, executables are inside `.app` bundles. To build and run tests:

```
cd tests && make -j 8 && ./tests.app/Contents/MacOS/tests
```

A single test is run by its name, `./tests.app/Contents/MacOS/tests "Log file is findable, clearable and rotated"`, which is what a negative control needs. The suite is registered with ctest as `arctic_engine_tests`, so `cd tests && make -j 8 && ctest` runs the same thing with the window kept off the screen and the working directory set for the test data; `ctest -R name` picks the suite out and `ctest --output-on-failure` shows which test failed.

Startup is `StartupMode { kWindowed, kHiddenWindow, kNoWindow }`, decided by the application through `ARCTIC_STARTUP_MODE_DECIDER` and overridable from the outside: `ARCTIC_HEADLESS=1` alone means a hidden window with a GL context, which is what a test run that draws needs, and `ARCTIC_HEADLESS=1 ARCTIC_DISABLE_HW=1` means no window, no GL context and no sound device at all, while `ARCTIC_DISABLE_AUDIO=1` alone only keeps the sound device closed.

The log is `log.txt` in the current directory, which on macOS is `Contents/Resources` inside the bundle; `LogFilePath()` says where it is, the first lines of every run say when it started and with what arguments, `SetLogSizeLimit` rotates it into `log_prev.txt`, and `ClearLog()` empties it. On Linux the build itself needs no ALSA: without it `ARCTIC_NO_ALSA` is defined, CMake prints a warning, and the program runs mute. The graphics backend is chosen with `-DARCTIC_GRAPHICS=auto|glx|gles`, and `auto` prefers GLX everywhere except a Raspberry Pi.
